<title>BELGIUM: Tractebel to sell French Cofira stake to CGE.</title>
<headline>Tractebel to sell French Cofira stake to CGE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian utility Tractebel said on Tuesday it was in talks with French Compagnie Generale des Eaux (CGE) about the sale of its 4.14 percent stake in CGE unit Cofira to CGE.</p>
<p>Cofira controls 80 percent of SFR, which owns and runs France's second mobile phone network.</p>
<p>The deal, when finalised, would result in an extraordinary profit of about three billion Belgian francs.  </p>
<p>Tractebel holds its Cofira stake via its 80 percent owned unit  Coditel, in which holding company Ackermans &amp; Van Haaren NV (AVH) has the other 20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
